Z||000000||corbz||08-31-99||02:28 PM||||Does anyone know if you can converte an 85 notchback to a fastback?<br>
Z||000001||four50four||08-31-99||02:49 PM||||try this link....  <A HREF="http://212.206.1.44/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000237.html" TARGET=_blank>http://212.206.1.44/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000237.html</A> 
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||08-31-99||03:22 PM||||There are 2 ways to do this, use the Pisa GTFX conversion<br> <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/fiero/gtfx.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/fiero/gtfx.htm</A> <br>or remove the back end and put on the fastback clip.<br> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html</A> 
Z||000003||Cooter||08-31-99||04:19 PM||||I did this conversion on my car and it was fairly simple. The only problem that I had was the tail light wiring- the notchback has combination turn signal/brake lights and the fastback has seperate amber turn signals and brake lights. Because of this, the wiring is VERY different, even though the light harness from the GT will plug into the notchback, it makes crazy stuff happen.
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||08-31-99||06:24 PM||||what kind of stuff?<p>If I can't find a reasonably priced GT I was seriously considering the fastback clip swap. However if it screws up the operation of the tail lights.. I'm not sure..
Z||000005||Cooter||08-31-99||09:07 PM||||All I had to do was leave the main part of the notchback's wiring harness in place and chop off the light sockets at the ends. I then spliced the GT light sockets into the notchback's harness. I spliced the light up "PONTIAC" on the tail lights into the park light circuit. The only really noticable thing about it is that the amber and red lights come on with the brakes and the red and amber blink with the turn signals. The way I see it, the back of the car is really lit up during braking so maybe the guy behind me won't ram me for the lack of brake lighting.
Z||000006||88 Fiero||08-31-99||09:13 PM||||Rewiring a notchback fiero to the fastback GT is not that bad. FOCOA magazine has an article about it on how to rewire the whole thing with pictures... e-mail and I will scan that picture and send you that article by e-mail.....
